# A BallVector with one-limb centers times a number a of T (milestone2.md, "BallVector":
# bv_scale_k): the centers by mul_1_1, entry by entry, as the map scale_1; the state that of
# norm_upper_1 on the centers written; the one radius bv_scale_radius_1 at the largest magnitude,
# the largest of the radii of ball_scale_1 entry by entry; norm_finish_1 tests that it is finite.
# When it is not (the operand is the whole space, a is not finite, or something overflowed), every
# center written is zero and the radius +infinity: the whole space.
fold:          bv_scale_1
arrays:        stored x
scalars:       stored rx, supplied a
state:         m, mask ok
step:          z = scale_step_1(x, a)
record:        (m, ok) = norm_step_1(m, ok, z)
combine:       (m, ok) = norm_combine(m, ok, m, ok)
radius:        rz = bv_scale_radius_1(m, rx, a)
finish:        (r, finite) = norm_finish_1(rz, ok)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z
output:        r
output:        mask finite
value:         x*a
requires:      ball_vector x rx
ensures:       encloses_entries z r x*a x=x,rx flag=finite finite_when=abs_le((abs(x)+rx)*a,-2) radii_when=abs_le(rx*a,-2)
min_precision: 1
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
source:        mul_1_1 on the centers, the radius of ball_scale_1 at the largest center (milestone2.md, BallVector)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
